# Elesh Norn, Mother of Machines stops abilities "of permanents your opponents control" - not an ability that functions
# from a graveyard (CR 603.2, 113.6). Bot2's Sword of the Meek is in Bot2's graveyard (its own Disenchant, turn 2); with
# Bot1's Elesh Norn out, Bot2's Llanowar Elves, a 1/1, enters on turn 4 and Sword of the Meek's "Whenever a 1/1 creature you
# control enters, you may return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield, then attach it to that creature" still
# triggers: Bot2 accepts and the Sword comes back on the Elves. Torpor Orb, which stops it, is the contrast
# (torpor-orb-stops-sword-of-the-meek-in-the-graveyard-for-a-one-one-entering).

